# Language and tone consistency

## Default language policy

- Default language for docs is English.
- Do not mix languages in the same page. All section headings and table headers must be in English.

## Tone policy

- Use technical, prescriptive, and neutral tone.
- Prioritize clarity and scanability over narrative style.
- Avoid marketing language, slogans, and subjective claims.
- Keep statements evidence-based (Figma, token JSON, explicit decisions).

## Writing style

- Prefer short paragraphs, bullets, and tables.
- Use active voice and direct instructions when describing usage.
- Use `TBD` instead of speculative wording.

## Capitalisation rules

### Headings

Use **Title Case** for all H2 and H3 headings — capitalise every major word. Articles (`a`, `an`, `the`), coordinating conjunctions (`and`, `but`, `or`), and prepositions ≤ 4 letters (`in`, `on`, `to`, `of`, `for`, `with`) are lower-case unless they are the first word.

| ✅ Correct | ❌ Incorrect |
|---|---|
| `## Usage Guidelines` | `## Usage guidelines` |
| `## Related Components` | `## Related components` |
| `## Visual Specifications` | `## Visual specifications` |
| `### Token Mapping` | `### Token mapping` |
| `### When to Use` | `### When to use` |
| `## Gaps / TBD` | `## Gaps / tbd` |

> **Why:** The canonical H2 names (`CANONICAL_H2_ORDER` in `tooling/lib/markdown-sections.json`) are defined in Title Case. Sentence-case variants create duplicate-section detection failures in `validate:docs`.

### Body text

Use **sentence case** everywhere else — in bullet points, table cells, labels, and prose. Capitalise only the first word and proper nouns.

| ✅ Correct | ❌ Incorrect |
|---|---|
| `Use for primary actions.` | `Use For Primary Actions.` |
| `Token: \`color/action/primary\`` | `Token: \`Color/Action/Primary\`` |
| `Figma node: \`Button/Primary\`` | `figma node: \`button/primary\`` |

### Acronyms and proper nouns

Always preserve the canonical casing of design system terms regardless of position:

| Term | Always written as |
|---|---|
| Design system name | `Iter` |
| App name | `Karmap` |
| Figma | `Figma` (never `figma` or `FIGMA`) |
| Token path segments | lower-case with slashes: `color/brand/primary` |
| ARIA attributes | upper-case: `aria-label`, `role` |
| `TBD` placeholder | always uppercase: `TBD` (never `tbd`, `Tbd`) |

## Tone violation examples

### Marketing language (forbidden)

| ❌ Violation | ✅ Replacement |
|---|---|
| `A beautifully crafted button component.` | `A button component with four visual variants.` |
| `Seamlessly integrates with your design system.` | `Consumes tokens from the Semantic collection.` |
| `Intuitive and delightful interactions.` | `Follows WCAG 2.1 AA keyboard navigation.` |
| `Simply the best choice for CTAs.` | `Recommended for primary call-to-action flows.` |

### Speculative wording (forbidden)

| ❌ Violation | ✅ Replacement |
|---|---|
| `This might support RTL in the future.` | `RTL behavior: \`TBD\`` |
| `We plan to add a loading variant soon.` | `Loading variant: \`TBD\`` |
| `Probably best used for primary actions.` | `Use for primary actions.` |
| `Could be used in modals as well.` | evidence-based or `TBD` |

### Passive / vague voice (avoid)

| ❌ Avoid | ✅ Prefer |
|---|---|
| `The button can be configured to...` | `Set \`Type\` to \`Primary\` to...` |
| `It is recommended to avoid...` | `Do not use...` |
| `Should be noted that...` | remove the hedge; state the rule |
